A||||4||GT Bastard||Good old fashion Mustang kill...||||2||
Z||000000||GT Bastard||10-07-2000||12:53 PM||||Now that everyone has voiced their opinions on street racing.... I pulled up next to a white 96ish Mustang GT 4.6 late last night. Pretty sure he was an auto... He kept edging his way ahead of me to attract attention.  I didn't intend to race him so we took off very slow together.  towards the middle of first gear he decides to punch it, and I figure I'll give him a run. I nailed it immediately after him so we started the race with me at his back bumper.  By the top of first gear we're DEAD EVEN. I hit second and I'm slowly pulling away.  We both shutdown with me about a car-length ahead of him. I've heard everyone say 4.6 Stang are pathetic, but this is the first race against one. I went home with a grin on my face last night.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">   <P>------------------<BR>Gold 86 SE V6 4-sp w/4.10 gears, Eibach springs, Koni's all around w/some poly bushings<BR>Yoko's<BR>Coated headers<BR>ACT 4-puck clutch<BR>MSD ignition<BR>Flowmaster w/ mandrel bent 2.5 pipe<BR>extrude honed intake<BR>Lots of fuel system mods... etc etc...||||reg||2
Z||000001||BBBAD GT||10-07-2000||03:04 PM||||Only the 96-98 4.6's are pathetic, espically the automatics.  Don't try this with a 1999+ 4.6, Ford finally came through with some respectable HP in 1999, but that probably won't stop you  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P><P>------------------<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://scribers.midwest.net/bbbad50/BBBAD_GT_SIG.gif">    <P><A HREF="http://scribers.midwest.net/bbbad50/V8Fiero" TARGET=_blank>BBBAD V8</A><P><A HREF="http://scribers.midwest.net/bbbad50/Fiero.htm" TARGET=_blank>BBBAD GT</A><P><A HREF="http://scribers.midwest.net/bbbad50/" TARGET=_blank>BBBAD 5.0</A>||||reg||1
Z||000002||My7Fieros||10-07-2000||09:43 PM||||Glad to hear about your kill, especially killing a mudstain...<BR>But, my roommate has a 98 Mudstain Gt convertible 5 spd....and I hate to admit it, but its anything but slow. It'll def. snap your head back.||||reg||14
Z||000003||GT Bastard||10-07-2000||09:47 PM||||Yeah, I've been in an older 5.0, 5sp and they're quick.  I can respect the kind of performance they give, but I don't care for the styling at all.  And they just seem to have clumsy handling...  ||||reg||1
Z||000004||ur2biteme||10-08-2000||12:58 AM||||i used to own a 94 v6 auto, and it wasn't that fast, but it wasn't a slouch either.  i have heard that the v6 handles better than the v8 for the same reason the duke fieros sometimes handle better than the v6:  better weight balance.  i'd say that they handle fairly well, but they sure arent a fiero  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  the power steering pump is overpowered and it gives the feeling of being sort of detached from the road, but it's a totally different beast after 85mph.  everything becomes more responsive and there is MUCH more road feel.  good cruzing car, and i plan on buying it back from my mom in about a year.  i need something with a backseat.  i'm keeping my fiero though.  <P>------------------<BR>UR2BITEME<BR>'87 econo coupe<BR>170k and a bad fender :(||||reg||1
